From: MastaG <mastag@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: defer BC-250 OD commits across DP link training

The interlock had a hole exactly where this board needs it. link_hdmi_frl.c
covers native HDMI FRL training, which a DP-out board never runs at all.
link_dpms.c covers the PCON's own autonomous HDMI-side training, which only
starts after the stream unblanks. Neither covers DP link training itself --
and that is what runs on every mode change.

So a forced RequestGfxclk/ForceGfxVid from cyan-skillfish-governor-smu could
still land in the middle of bringing the link up, which is what kept killing
a KDE <-> gamescope switch: picture lost, link left at 0 lanes / 0 rate, and
no modeset ever reaching the post-unblank window to be deferred by.

Established on hardware rather than inferred. With the governor running, the
switch into gamescope (4K120, DSC, HBR2) lost signal every time, and across
seven modesets the post-unblank window never once observed a commit to defer
-- the commits were landing where nothing was watching. With
cyan-skillfish-governor-smu stopped and nothing else writing
pp_od_clk_voltage, the same switch works reliably in both directions.

Bracket perform_link_training_with_retries() with the same flag the other two
sites use, so the SMU side needs no change. A wrapper rather than set/clear
inside the body: it returns from three places inside a retry loop, and an
early return that skipped the clear would leave OD commits refused forever.
Nesting is not handled (the clear is unconditional, matching link_hdmi_frl.c)
because DC brings up one link at a time here, and the HDMI FRL path never runs
on this board.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_training.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_training.c
@@ -48,6 +48,17 @@
 #include "resource.h"
 #include "dm_helpers.h"
 
+#include <linux/atomic.h>
+
+/*
+ * Shared with drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_hdmi_frl.c
+ * and drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/cyan_skillfish_ppt.c -- see the
+ * comment in link_hdmi_frl.c for why Cyan Skillfish's OD clock/voltage commit
+ * path needs to defer around a link that is being brought up.
+ */
+extern atomic_t cs_hdmi_frl_training_active;
+extern bool cs_od_defer_debug;
+
 #define DC_LOGGER \
 	link->ctx->logger
 
@@ -1617,7 +1628,7 @@
 	return status;
 }
 
-bool perform_link_training_with_retries(
+static bool cs_perform_link_training_with_retries_inner(
 	const struct dc_link_settings *link_setting,
 	bool skip_video_pattern,
 	int attempts,
@@ -1816,3 +1827,50 @@
 	return false;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Cyan Skillfish: hold off OD clock/voltage commits for as long as a DP link
+ * is being brought up.
+ *
+ * This is the third and, on a DP-out board, the decisive place the interlock
+ * is needed. link_hdmi_frl.c covers native HDMI FRL training, which a DP-out
+ * board never runs; link_dpms.c covers the PCON's own autonomous HDMI-side
+ * training, which only begins after the stream unblanks. Neither covers DP
+ * link training itself -- and that is what runs on every mode change, which
+ * is where a forced RequestGfxclk/ForceGfxVid was still killing the link.
+ * Established on hardware: with cyan-skillfish-governor-smu stopped, a
+ * KDE <-> gamescope switch that otherwise lost signal every time works
+ * reliably, while the post-unblank window in link_dpms.c never once observed
+ * a commit to defer.
+ *
+ * A wrapper rather than set/clear inside the body: the body returns from
+ * three places inside a retry loop, and an early return that skipped the
+ * clear would leave OD commits refused forever. Nesting is not handled (the
+ * clear is unconditional, matching link_hdmi_frl.c) because DC brings up one
+ * link at a time here, and on this board the HDMI FRL path never runs at all.
+ */
+bool perform_link_training_with_retries(
+	const struct dc_link_settings *link_setting,
+	bool skip_video_pattern,
+	int attempts,
+	struct pipe_ctx *pipe_ctx,
+	enum signal_type signal,
+	bool do_fallback)
+{
+	bool ret;
+
+	atomic_set(&cs_hdmi_frl_training_active, 1);
+	if (cs_od_defer_debug)
+		pr_info("amdgpu: cs_od_defer: DP link training started, deferring OD clock/voltage commits\n");
+
+	ret = cs_perform_link_training_with_retries_inner(link_setting,
+							  skip_video_pattern,
+							  attempts, pipe_ctx,
+							  signal, do_fallback);
+
+	atomic_set(&cs_hdmi_frl_training_active, 0);
+	if (cs_od_defer_debug)
+		pr_info("amdgpu: cs_od_defer: DP link training finished (%s), OD clock/voltage commits allowed\n",
+			ret ? "ok" : "failed");
+
+	return ret;
+}
